## Implementation Summary

### Files Created

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `app/server.py` | Flask backend — orchestrates Anserini CLI commands for setup, search, evaluation |
| `app/index.html` | Single-page dashboard UI with readiness panel, live search, evaluation metrics, commands/artifacts |
| `app/requirements.txt` | Python dependencies (Flask, gunicorn) |
| `Dockerfile` | Docker image based on `eclipse-temurin:21-jdk` with Python 3 |
| `run.sh` | Entrypoint that downloads fatjar if needed and starts the server |
| `tests/test_browser.py` | Playwright end-to-end browser test |
| `README.md` | Documentation with Docker/Render deployment instructions |
| `.gitignore` | Excludes runtime data, jars, caches |

### Architecture

- **Backend**: Python Flask that shells out to real Anserini CLI commands (`io.anserini.cli.Search`, `SearchCollection`, `TrecEval`, `ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes`)
- **Setup flow** (background thread at startup):
  1. Verify Java 21
  2. Download Anserini fatjar from Maven Central
  3. Run CACM smoke test
  4. Discover NFCorpus reproduction config via `--dry-run`
  5. Discover NFCorpus topics
  6. Run `SearchCollection` for NFCorpus BM25
  7. Evaluate with `TrecEval`, compare observed nDCG@10 (0.3218) vs expected
- **Live search**: Each query runs `io.anserini.cli.Search --json` against `beir-v1.0.0-nfcorpus.flat` prebuilt index
- **Evaluation**: Observed nDCG@10 matches expected value (0.3218) — **PASS** ✅
- **No mocking**: All results come from real Anserini commands

### Key NFCorpus Configuration (from `beir.core` reproduction YAML)
- **Prebuilt Index**: `beir-v1.0.0-nfcorpus.flat` (~6.2 MB, 3,633 docs)
- **Topics**: `beir-nfcorpus` (323 queries)
- **Qrels**: `beir-v1.0.0-nfcorpus.test`
- **Expected nDCG@10**: 0.3218